{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter and Online Dating", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Let Me Tell You What Happened ... ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use relative clauses when you want to make it clear which person or thing  you are talking about.<br/><br/>  The relative pronouns <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> and <span class=\"italic\">that</span> begin a relative clause.  <br><span class=\"italic\">who</span> refers to people<br> <span class=\"italic\"> which</span> refers to things <br><span class=\"italic\"> that</span> refers to either people or things<br/><br/>  In conversation, you usually use<span class=\"italic\"> that</span>,  rather than  <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or  <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.<br/><br/>  You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"underline\">subject relative clause</span> describes the <span class=\"strong\">subject</span> of the clause.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The person who texted me wanted to know where I was.</span><br/> Which person? The person who texted me.<br/> The clause <span class=\"italic\">who texted me</span> follows <span class=\"italic\">person</span> - the noun it describes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An <span class=\"underline\">object relative clause</span> describes the <span class=\"strong\">object </span>of the clause. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Could you give me the mug that is over there?</span><br/> Which mug? The mug that is over there.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Relative Pronoun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Type of Relative Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Laughter is the thing which gets people most comfortable on a first date. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" which gets people most comfortable on a first date\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">which</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I've met several girls online who thought that our conversations were amusing.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" who thought that our conversations were amusing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">who</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">object</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The first bar that we went to was too loud.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" that we went to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> They were entertained by the things that I was writing.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that I was writing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">object</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way.  <br/><br/> You use Present Perfect Continuous tense to describe:  <ul><li>a single activity that lasts a long time, and</li><li>  an action that is repeated over a long period of time.</li></ul> ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about experience. When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous</span> tense when a long activity has just stopped.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To emphasize the <span class=\"underline\">action</span>, use the continuous form.<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>I've been wanting to write to you for a while now.</li><li> I have been talking to this girl for a few days.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To emphasize the <span class=\"underline\">result </span>of the action, use the simple form.<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Something might have changed since last week.</li><li> So far, my first dates have been a disaster!</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Has/Have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb+ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wanting to write <span class=\\\"strong\\\">for</span> a while now.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  talking to this girl <span class=\\\"strong\\\">since</span> Monday.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " <ul><li>You use FOR to talk about how long an action has been happening (a week, 2 days, five hours, six years, etc.). </li><li>You use SINCE to talk about when the action started (2010, Monday, she was a child).  </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I've been wanting to write to you for a while now, but I've been so busy with life and work lately!", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I have been talking to this girl since Monday, and we have so many things in common! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "amusing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to entertain", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've met several girls online who thought that our conversations were amusing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to describe a date.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "entertained", "type": "name"}, {"content": " feeling enjoyment and amusement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was so excited to know that they were entertained by the things that I was writing. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "laughter", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the action and sound of laughing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally always says that laughter is very important on a date.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tiring", "type": "name"}, {"content": " causing someone to feel exhausted", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It felt like a very awkward and tiring evening.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in common", "type": "name"}, {"content": "sharing many interests", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have been talking to this girl, and we have so many things in common! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "knackered", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extremely tired (British English)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: By the time I came home I was knackered, as Vanessa says.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "out of my league", "type": "name"}, {"content": "I don't feel good or adequate enough for a person I like romantically", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I met a very nice girl last night. I just hope she's not out of my league.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a dialogue (12-14 lines) with a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose between 2 characters. The first character has something very important to say. It can be funny, incredible, something about a relationship, etc. ...", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The second character asks questions and wants to know more details.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember to use the Present Perfect and Present Perfect Continuous tenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember to use relative clauses for long sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange roles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about complex subjects in long sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about feelings, reactions and social activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I role-play a dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about social activities, feelings and reactions. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things I have been doing and things I have done. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express complex statements using words like who, that or which.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How long have you known your best friend?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How long do you think it takes to know someone well? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " It's been an interesting couple of weeks&